35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, the readmission data is encouraging, but the ledger shows our allocation is down nearly a quarter. We must be realistic about what we can actually fund.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, the readmission drop proves the model works. The booking system’s gaps are the real threat to its sustainability, not the ledger.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, the staffing review shows therapy is bleeding staff, but midwifery has unusual slack. @Shizue, the board minutes confirm the joint clinic failed because neither department owned the rota.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that midwifery slack is a relief, but the rooms are already full by mid-morning. We physically cannot fit another daily program without overbooking.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, exactly. The shared round lost a third of its visits to weather and locked gates. We cannot repeat that failure with a new program.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, the booking gaps are critical, but the financial cut is immediate. We cannot build a program that the ledger simply cannot support.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, the ledger is a constraint, not a verdict. If the booking system can’t track the work, the program dies regardless of the budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, you’re right that tracking is vital, but the therapy staffing review shows four years of physiotherapists leaving. We can’t staff a unit that’s already hemorrhaging talent.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, the staffing loss is real, but the booking system only holds named slots. If we can’t log the work, it vanishes from every report.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, the booking gaps are a symptom. The real failure was the shared round losing a third of visits to weather and locked gates.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, the weather is a factor, but the ledger is the wall. We must pick a program that fits the reduced budget and existing staff, not just the ideal.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, the ledger limits scale, not viability. If the booking system can’t track the work, the program dies regardless of the budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, the budget is tight, but the staffing review shows midwifery has unusual slack. We should leverage that capacity rather than ignoring it.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that slack is useful, but the car park fills before eleven. We physically cannot absorb more daily traffic without seizing up.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, the car park is a daily headache, but the shared round’s failure was about ownership, not parking. We must ensure one department truly commits this time.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the midwifery slack is a genuine asset. @Shion, if the booking system can track it, we have a viable path forward despite the ledger.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, the midwifery slack is a distraction. The booking system’s inability to track unslotted work is the fatal flaw. We must fix that first.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, you’re right that tracking is vital, but the midwifery slack is a genuine asset. We should leverage that capacity rather than ignoring it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Shion, I agree the booking gaps are dangerous, but the car park filling before eleven is a hard physical limit. We cannot schedule what we cannot physically house.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, the booking system is a tool, not the foundation. The shared round failed because no one owned the rota. We must secure that commitment before worrying about software.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
